      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand wanting to clean and close the wound quickly, but it's really risky to use superglue on a wound. It can cause severe tissue damage and doesn't have enough antimicrobial properties. Instead, here's how you can safely manage the wound: Clean the wound once more and apply antibiotic ointment. Cover with a clean bandage or gauze and hypoallergenic tape. This helps keep the area clean and protected without risking more injury. If your wound seems unmanageable, bleeding persistently, or if you notice signs of infection, seeking professional medical help is very important. Sometimes, visiting a healthcare provider can be quicker than you think, even with an upcoming project deadline. They're trained to handle such situations, and their quick intervention can save you from long-term complications. If the area is too gaping, wrap with a clean cloth first; it'll help despite not being as immediate as superglue, it's much safer. And remember, a neater, safer dressing is better than risking more harm. Please be cautious, especially with an open cut where dirt and bacteria could cause an infection.",
